; TeX-Assigns: what TeX needs; nothing is copied into the system.
; Used by the TeX-Shell.  To have TeX in every Shell, put these two lines
; into S:User-Startup (with your path):
;   Assign TeX: Work:TeX
;   Execute TeX:S/TeX-Assigns
Assign >NIL: EXISTS TeX:
If WARN
  Echo "TeX-Assigns: TeX: is not assigned."
  Quit 10
EndIf

; ixemul.library: the copy in TeX:Libs is found after LIBS:.  An older
; ixemul in LIBS: would be found first and is too old for these programs.
If NOT "$TeXLibsAdded" EQ "yes"
  Assign LIBS: TeX:Libs ADD
  SetEnv TeXLibsAdded yes
EndIf
Version >NIL: ixemul.library 80
If WARN
  Echo "TeX: ixemul.library in LIBS: is older than version 80."
  Echo "     Copy TeX:Libs/ixemul.library and ixnet.library to LIBS:."
EndIf

; ixemul asks for the volume AmiTCP: if it does not exist.  A TCP stack
; normally provides it; otherwise any directory will do.
Assign >NIL: EXISTS AmiTCP:
If WARN
  Assign AmiTCP: TeX:
EndIf

Path TeX:bin/m68k-amigaos ADD
